  I'm playing NH 3.0p7 on an IBM PC/XT. I haven't upgraded to 3.0p9
because I've a good game going, and I heard that old files are
unusable with the new version. I tried to start nh up this morning,
but the program crashed on me. I've occasionally gotten similar errors
during play, so I copy the save file every time I quit.

  I'm a 30th lvl wizard, I've explored 22 levels, and I was
constructing a poly pile on the 6th level beside an altar. The pile
was 12 pages long, mostly armor. I saved the file last night, and made
a copy of it (overwriting my last backup of it). The save file is
182137 bytes long.

  I tried to start it up this morning, and it began to load it up,
saying that there were 22 levels, read them all in without complaint,
then instead of starting, it cleared the screen and displayed:

Suddenly, the dungeon collapses.
ERROR:  Cannot get 47 bytes--More--
                                   Abnormal program termination

C>

(Of course I'd typed return after the --More--).

  on my hard disk there are files called LEVELS.1 through LEVELS.22
except LEVELS.6. The size of the save file minus the size of the
LEVELS files is 26489 bytes.

  The error is unfortunately very repeatable, with the identical error
message each time. 

  Any help would be greatly appreciated, as I've been working on this
game for 3 weeks so far.

						Neil


